PRO-FORMA FIRST BOARD OF DIRECTORS RESOLUTION OF [●] WFOE LIMITED

The undersigned, being all the duly appointed members of the first board of directors of [●] WFOE Limited (the “Company”), a wholly foreign-owned enterprise to be incorporated under the laws of China, do hereby waive notice and consent to and adopt the following resolutions at a meeting duly held on [date]:

RESOLVED, that the registered share capital of the Company shall be USD [●] or its RMB equivalent, divided into [●] ordinary shares with a par value of USD [●] each, and that each founding shareholder is authorized and directed to subscribe for the number of shares set opposite such shareholder’s name in the share register and to contribute the subscribed capital to the Company’s designated capital contribution account in cash or in kind, in accordance with the Articles of Association and the Capital Contribution Schedule approved by this Board, no later than [●];

RESOLVED, that the registered office address of the Company shall be [address], and the Company Secretary or General Manager is hereby authorized to execute any lease, license, or certification documents required by the State Administration for Market Regulation or local authorities, and to effect any changes upon Company approval;

RESOLVED, that the Company shall open one or more bank accounts with licensed commercial banks in China; the Chairman/General Manager, Chief Financial Officer, and [●] are designated as primary signatories; all cheques, drafts, wire instructions and payment orders shall be valid when signed by any two authorized signatories, with exceptions for sole-signature transactions in compliance with regulatory thresholds;

RESOLVED, that the Company hereby appoints [●] as General Manager and Chief Executive Officer, [●] as Chief Financial Officer, and [●] as Company Secretary and Compliance Officer, each with powers, salaries and duties set out in the employment agreements and the Articles of Association;

RESOLVED, that [●] is appointed as the statutory representative and Chairman, with full power to execute all governmental filings, licensing applications, contracts and banking documents incidental to the organization and operation of the Company, and the Board authorizes the Company Secretary to stamp the Company seal, issue certifications, and certify deed; and

RESOLVED, that all actions previously taken by incorporation agents, counsel and officers in connection with the formation of the Company, including filing the Articles of Association and obtaining the business license, are hereby ratified, confirmed and approved, and the officers are directed to fulfil all post-registration obligations, including bank activation, tax registration, social insurance registration, and any regulatory licensing requirements before commencing production.
